  {
   "id": "crush-annotations-md-5",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Hyphenated keys such as `revisit-if` and `expires-when` parse (an old `crushc`\nhang on `revisit-if`, crush-ast #38, is fixed). An `@invariant`'s `check` is\nstored, not executed. (`crushc --invariant-runtime` emits calls to an\n`invariant.evaluate` capability at the top of each targeted function, but\n`crush-run` does not provide one, so such a program is refused: `not available in\nthis host: invariant.evaluate`.)\n\n## The AI-native statements\n\nCAST has AI nodes (queries, tool chains, agent delegation, goals, …) for programs\nthat agents emit as JSON; they are described in [AI-Native CAST](https://docs.crushlang.org/cast/ai-native.html).\nTwo of them also have Crush built-ins, `ai_semantic_match(text, target,\nthreshold)` and `ai_synthesize(prompt)`, which compile to the same\ncapability-gated call as the CAST `SemanticMatch` / `Synthesize` nodes. `crush-run`\nhas no AI backend, so such a program is refused before it runs; a host that\nprovides `ai_native.semantic_match` can run it:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-annotations-3",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    let m = ai_semantic_match(\"refund\", \"billing\", 0.8)\n    print(m)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
